        <p>Conyere argument appeared to convince !dun IN olds°, She yielded ...mit to all hie wild., " Let us go in now," wed the younA nian. •• I Want to declare our engagement to the earl." He drew her arm in ha, and they returned to the drawing-rrram. They found Lord Hawk horst ant Mr. Callender waiting for them. Conyers to I the girl forward to the earl, and raid, with unmistakable triumph " My lord, you will nee that I have followed the prompting. of my heart and your own exprefted "mho. Permit me to present to you my promieed wife." The earl looked his amazement. " This is quiek work," he raid, smiling. "I am very much pleased, (Mari, very tiototi plavird, Rollyn. I hope you two will be hapoy. I am glad that the daughter of my old fi bald will be the mistress of Hawks' Cliff when Inn: goo.. Ile kissed Miss Woulsor very gra...folly, and congratulated Conyers with a genuine delight. Mr. Callender offered hi. congralulalmong. It wan twelve o'clork when tlie cragthorpe carriage wee ordered and Conyers emcorted M Windsor flown the steps. Ile put her into Ilia carriage carefully, tacking the ruge about her, and exacting. Isla what,.</p>
