      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1897-10-22_WidnesExaminer_art0021" n="art0021">
        <head>LADIES' LETIER.</head>
        <p>LADIES' LETIER.</p>
        <p>MT PLR NaLLIE, - The headgear of the moment is for the moat party pretty, but 1 honestly confeas that although charming in themselves, 1 would infinitely prefer them to be trirnmed with ostrich feather, notiues' plumes, or wings, instead of with large corpses of defunct fowls. To put • dead body in • hat offends my utile. Firstly, it mem. to me horrible to put an end to my living creature without some good reason. and although you may argue that it cannot matter to a seagull, if it has to be killed at all, whether it is slain to complete a °olfaction in • mwoum, tfr that its mangled remains shall adorn (1) some silly woman's hat ;nih the cruelty exists ell the same.</p>
        <p>It). very faihionable tn wear largo hate tilted MI 006 side. Where the hat is worn on one side the hair Mon hi be domed low, while where tilted on the nom li' horihulif he ',milled up on to the crown. Anog the enlist test ehapeaus this autumn are those of beaveroeiloured unrolr velvet, or the new beaver eatin, • f stiric very inuch like the old bets worn hy highwaymen. These materials aro drown over is 'Mope trimmed with some fluffy net, bunches of dark ostrich feathers, and a profmion of white plumee above them. The newest ostrich leather hail no curl at all in it. It hange nn a introir velvet beret, with the smartest air plaudit°, though bobornitin rooovte.l it, in se dejected look. log Be any fiosther that has been init in a ehower. Almost all the coats are Russian in style, and almost all the drese bodice.; are pouched and belted. appear to be narrower, though, in reality, thief are ipiite wi fell but they are out rittiA very closely round the hips. and all the Whims bretowed at the back.</p>
        <p>A eery horoming coat has a double-breasted front And !anent+ at the left sole with two buttons. It I. pouched rlightly in front over the warithatol, but it in plain and tighfitting at tildes and hack, while many vows of stitching give. a Man finieh to the 1111011 'moque, the pointed lapeln to the high mediei collar. The last touch to the 11.4 IS a eollar•liand and yoke of satin tinely tucked. Russian belted coats of seal or astrachan are fashionable, and the orthodox plain sealnkin jacket is still worn, while for then° people who prefer for cape. to coat, there is any amount of rape. to choose from. The only new thing shout them latter is that they are mmtly insole with very high collar., and that ROMs ivory 1.11 is Les LowsLl about them notnewhere.</p>
        <p>Superb Rarmian mate of 1,14e1K velours de Nord bring., to tire realities of winter. fhoi 1 now lively was a oUo and handsome garinent, well suited to tall slender li4ures or to the petite riiong4 or. 'The high st...nn callar and cuffs are with skunk, which fur ids° coven the Intoning et to. solo, and descends from the shimider t.i rite w ilet. ellen it is loot in • ben., belt of cut p The coat on the losok hiis a box pleat at Lock, coining out to wider pleats on Olin barque. Drtioi ito!iio, aro so est end trimmed just now ploys oiol Lbw. ) that the umoal fastenings of close huttonholee are not feasible</p>
