        <p>The annual taretines of the Unitest Kingdom Alliance were held in Mans,l,seter Tueedar. Sir Wilfrid La ar- nressided over the Council nieetiog in the morning, and t,rl Battersea t,..11 the chair at the great pubis, meeting In the evening in the Yree Trade Hall. In to. ity and onthusianal marked the proceeding* td both ostJutringa. ftreolutiona wet. ad ,pted declaring the dealt traffic to he productive of great evil, and calling for an At to he pasted by the Isegislature enabling the inhabitants Wally 1, prdobit the aale of inh,atuting liquor. in defined localitiee. rhe new Prime Minister of Natal i• the son of • once weed known Quaker minister. Hui father, the late Mr. Henry limns. he'd f years In Sunderland, and Wised thence hi Croydon, where he dled a toe years agc. Mr. Henry Pions, on , oettled in Natal • number uf yes.. lago, leaving England partly feheslth. sake.</p>
