        <p>Onion OF Llierrisis•NT-COLOWIL Tun Hon. Cli•lthies POWYS. The death is announced of Llent.-Colonel the Hon. Charles Powys, late of the 9th Lancers. lie was eon of the second Lord Lilford and was born in 1813. Prior to entering the Army he served five year, and three months in the Royal Navy, and Was present in Her Majesty's ship Blonde at the taking of the Mores Castle. in the Self of Lepanto. in 182$. He serv.sl with the 9th Lancers in the campaign of 1848-49 in the Punjab, including the palisage of the Chenab at Ramnuggar and the Battles of Chillian- wallah and Goojsrat. DlMMilfra.—CA IRO erraNIST V. LIVRISPOOL 9011TH NNW The Cairo-street Club commenced their season on Saturday, by paying a •isit to Liverpool North Red. Although they were defeated they did very well, considering the renown of their opponents. Score : CAIRO-W.IM LIVIORPOOI.. N. IR D W Tomlalnson O ToOlin II Olden Fred Wright II it Plinio.. Frans Wright 4 li F Johnsonsnsorn Total 74 Total lO. Mn. B. A. N•TLOS AND TON Llrl.lll Mr. R. • Naylor. of Cuerden Hall. Thelwall, again extended his kind invitation to the members of H iLynini) Company 3rd V B Cheahire Regiment, and on Saturday. headed by the band, the company marched to Iluerden Rail, where they were made welcome, and spent a very enjoyable afternoon.</p>
